                <pb facs="1691" n="1533" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1533"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Swiss Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Switzerland</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington, D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-02-08"><hi rendition="#italic">February 8,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: Giving effect to the
                    wish expressed in 1899 by the International Conference of The Hague, the Swiss
                    Federal Council invited, on the 17th of February, 1903, all the states
                    signatories of the convention of the 22d of August, 1864, for the amelioration
                    of the condition of wounded soldiers in armies in the field, to participate in a
                    conference which would be held at Geneva <pb facs="1692" n="1534"
                        xml:id="pg1534"/> on the 14th of September, 1903, for the purpose of
                    revising said convention. On the 24th of July, 1903, I had the honor to notify
                    your excellency that the said conference had been postponed to a more propitious
                    time.</p>
                <p>Now, all obstacles to the realization of the wish of the Conference of The Hague
                    being removed, the Federal Council has determined to invite anew the conference
                    for the 16th of May next at Geneva.</p>
                <p>By direction of my Government, I have, therefore, the honor to invite the
                    Government of the United States of America to take part in the deliberations of
                    this conference, and to be good enough to communicate to me its decision, as
                    well as the names of its delegates, by the end of the month of March next at
                    latest.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. du Martheray.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
